<title>ESTONIA: HOIUPANK'S 1Q PROFIT SOARS.</title>
<headline>HOIUPANK'S 1Q PROFIT SOARS.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonia's Hoiupank said on Wednesday that its first quarter net profit soared to 40.234 million kroons versus 11.074 million kroons in the same period last year.</p>
<p>The bank also said that its net profit in March rose to 14.2 million kroons from 12.51 million kroons.</p>
<p>&quot;Hoiupank has the fastest profit potential in Estonia, and this has been confirmed by our results,&quot; Priit Haller, the vice-chairman of the bank's board, said at a news conference.</p>
<p>He added that the bank's total assets in the first three months of the year grew to 5.03 billion kroons from 4.3 billion kroons.</p>
<p>The bank is the second largest in Estonia and had a net profit in 1996 of 64.78 million kroons.</p>
<p>--Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom +372 6 308400</p>
</text>
